    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/24007415/pediatric-nephrologist-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Pediatric Nephrologist",
      "description": "Pediatric Nephrologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Pediatric Nephrologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 195567 Pediatric Nephrologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 980455 Category: Faculty and Physicians 24007415 Responsibilities Position Overview UT Southwestern Medical Center (UTSW) and Children’s Health seek a visionary pediatric nephrologist to serve as Medical Director of Kidney Transplant. The Director will lead one of the largest, most established pediatric kidney transplant programs in the country, serving a diverse population across Texas and the region. The ideal candidate combines clinical excellence, a strong academic record, and proven leadership to advance the program’s innovation, outcomes, research, and collaboration. The Opportunity Working with the Solid Organ Transplant team, hospital administration, and medical leadership, the Director oversees the program’s clinical, quality, patient experience, and administrative priorities. The role centers on long-term patient outcomes, program growth, and a stronger regional and national reputation. Key collaborators include the Kidney Transplant Surgeon, the Pediatric Nephrology Division Chief and faculty, and Solid Organ Transplant Program (SOTP) leadership and staff. Key Responsibilities Clinical leadership and quality • Partner with the Surgical Program Director on clinical leadership and strategy, including review of adverse events and complications. • Champion best practices and set quality, safety, and patient experience standards aligned with Children’s Health and UTSW goals. • Update pre- and post-transplant guidelines to minimize rejection, infection, and comorbidities. • Benchmark outcomes against SRTR data with the surgical, nephrology, nursing, and quality teams. • Chair the bi-weekly Renal Transplant Selection Committee. • Supervise advanced practice providers (APPs) in the outpatient transplant clinic. Regulatory compliance and operations • Ensure compliance with UNOS, CMS, other regulators, and medical staff bylaws; lead accreditation. • Contribute to risk management, budgeting, and equipment and technology decisions. • Use data to improve efficiency and patient satisfaction. • Advocate for adequate staffing and psychosocial support that helps patients thrive into adulthood. Team leadership and education • Recruit, onboard, and mentor faculty, coordinators, nurses, and APPs, and support trainee education in the Division of Pediatric Nephrology. • Ensure appropriate credentialing, training, and scope of practice for all transplant providers. Strategy, research, and outreach • Collaborate with hospital leadership and institutional partners to advance program development and patient-centered care. • Grow referrals and shorten referral-to-listing time. • Drive research, clinical trials, quality improvement projects, and collaborative networks such as IROC. • Represent UTSW and Children’s Health at national and international forums. • Serve as primary physician contact for referring partners in Texas and the surrounding region; support marketing and media efforts. Qualifications • MD or DO, board certified in Pediatric Nephrology. • Eligible for Texas medical licensure and Children’s Health Medical Staff membership. • Three or more years of post-fellowship experience in pediatric kidney transplantation. • Transplant leadership or directorship experience strongly preferred. • Excellence in clinical care, teaching, research, and/or quality improvement. • Strong communication and team-building skills. • Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in healthcare. Apply at jobs.utsouthwestern.edu with your CV and a letter of interest. Benefits details: UTSW HR Resources . UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Linkedin Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees Let’s Get Started Join Talent Community Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Previous Next Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME 