    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/24000775/vice-chair-of-research-ophthalmology-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Vice Chair of Research - Ophthalmology",
      "description": "Vice Chair of Research - Ophthalmology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Vice Chair of Research - Ophthalmology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 195461 Vice Chair of Research – Ophthalmology Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 981330 Category: Faculty and Physicians 24000775 Responsibilities The Vice Chair of Research will provide strategic leadership to advance the Department of Ophthalmology’s research mission in ophthalmology and vision science. Reporting to the Department Chair and working closely with other departmental and institutional leaders, the Vice Chair will develop and implement a strategic plan for the continued growth of the Department’s research enterprise, expand extramural funding and philanthropic support, recruit and mentor research faculty, and accelerate discoveries that advance the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of eye disease. The incoming Vice Chair will assume this important leadership role at a time of dramatic growth for the Department of Ophthalmology, which has expanded significantly in faculty, physical space, support, and resources over the past few years. In this role, they will build upon the Department’s nationally recognized excellence in vision research, anchored by a National Eye Institute (NEI) P30 Vision Research Core Facility (with shared resources in stem cell and organoid biology, gene editing, viral vector production, advanced microscopy, and animal phenotyping), a Research to Prevent Blindness (RPB) Challenge Grant, and well-equipped basic science laboratories. Depending on the qualifications and accomplishments of the selected candidate, they may be eligible for an endowed chair and additional research support and resources to advance the candidate’s research program and the Department’s broader research mission. Key Responsibilities · Define and execute a bold strategic vision for the Department’s research programs. · Recruit, mentor , and retain outstanding research faculty, fostering an environment that supports innovation, collaboration, and sustained success. · Expand and diversify the Department’s portfolio of externally funded research through federal, foundation, and philanthropic support. · Lead and oversee the competitive renewal of the NEI P30 Vision Research Core Grant, oversee the RPB Challenge Grant, and direct the upcoming application for an RPB Unrestricted Grant. · Steward departmental research resources through strategic oversight of budgets, spending, laboratory space, and shared infrastructure, working with institutional research offices to strengthen grant administration and ensure compliance. · Forge strategic collaborations across UT Southwestern, drawing on its exceptional scientific strengths, to position the Department as a leading hub for vision science research. · Strengthen the scientific distinction of the Department’s research program by leading the annual Southwestern Vision Science Summit, Vision Science Seminar series, and other scientific programs. · Collaborate with education leadership to expand meaningful research opportunities for undergraduate, graduate, and medical students. · Track, evaluate , and elevate departmental research performance using clear measures of grant funding, publication impact, faculty development, and national recognition. · Champion the Department’s research mission within UT Southwestern and nationally through institutional committees, strategic initiatives, federal agencies, foundations, and professional organizations. Ideal Candidate Profile and Qualifications · PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent doctoral degree. · Eligible for appointment as an Associate Professor or Professor at UT Southwestern. · Nationally or internationally recognized leader in vision science or a closely related field. · Record of sustained extramural funding, including NIH or equivalent peer-reviewed support. · Strong record of high-impact publications and scientific achievement. · Experience leading successful research programs, shared resources, and research infrastructure. · Proven success mentoring laboratory-based research faculty. · Demonstrated success building collaborative research teams and shared research infrastructure. · Excellent leadership, communication, and organizational skills. · Commitment to advancing innovation, collaboration, mentorship, and excellence in ophthalmic and vision research. Application Process Interested candidates should submit the following to OphthalCareers@utsouthwestern.edu : · Current Curriculum Vitae (CV) · Letter of Interest outlining research accomplishments, leadership experience, and vision for advancing the Department of Ophthalmology’s research mission. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Linkedin Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees Let’s Get Started Join Talent Community Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Previous Next Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. Brenda Edwards Licensed Clinical Social Worker UT Southwestern is a great place to work and learn. Innovation and creativity to improve the quality of patient care are encouraged. Leadership within my team and department is supportive. Denise Anderson Denise Anderson GME Coordinator I I love working at UT Southwestern because of its great staff and great benefits. Everyday is extraordinary because there’s opportunity to expand your knowledge and advance your career. Navigation Home Why Work Here Locations Life in Dallas Benefits Job Search Results Sitemap Departments Advanced Practice Providers Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Residencies & Fellowships Quick Links Patient Care Research Education & Training Newsroom About Us UTSW Corporate Home Address 6001 Forest Park Road Suite NG3.111 Dallas, Texas 75235 Phone 214-648-9810 Annual Security Report (ASR) This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community. As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. © 2024 UT Southwestern Medical Center | All Rights Reserved Opens in a new window Patient Rights Open Records Privacy Policy Site Policies - powered by Enfold-Hodes-Accessible WordPress Theme We use cookies to improve and personalize your experience and to analyze website performance and traffic. Please see our Cookie Policy for a description of how we use cookies or to manage your settings. Accept Scroll to top"
