      "description": "Instructor - Molecular Medicine - Dr. Andrew Wang's Lab job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Instructor - Molecular Medicine - Dr. Andrew Wang's Lab job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 195229 Instructor – Molecular Medicine – Dr. Andrew Wang's Lab Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 980255 Category: Faculty and Physicians 23999482 Responsibilities An Instructor position is available immediately in the Section of Molecular Medicine within the Department of Radiation Oncology at The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center. The Section of Molecular Medicine’s mission is to educate and train the next cadre of scientists and clinicians in the disciplines of radiation and cancer biology and to execute a multidisciplinary program of research focused on understanding the molecular, cellular, and organismal responses to ionizing radiation exposure for the betterment of humankind. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to o