    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23982018/leukemia-specialist-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Leukemia Specialist",
      "description": "Leukemia Specialist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 195291 Leukemia Specialist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 980365 Category: Faculty and Physicians 23982018 Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Hematology and Oncology, is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor with a focused clinical and academic interest in Leukemia and Allogeneic Stem Cell Transplantation. The selected candidate will participate in clinical activities within Hematology and Oncology, including inpatient and outpatient care, and will contribute to the education and mentorship of medical students, residents, and fellows. Applicants must possess an M.D. degree or equivalent from an LCME-accredited medical school and have successfully completed an ACGME-accredited Internal Medicine residency program. Completion of fellowship training in Hematology and/or Oncology is required. Candidates must have specialized training and experience in the inpatient and outpatient evaluation and management of patients undergoing stem cell transplantation, with a particular emphasis on allogeneic transplant and leukemia care. Applicants must be board certified in Internal Medicine and eligible for Texas medical licensure. Board certification in Medical Oncology and/or Hematology is preferred. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and w