y members that work well in a collegial fashion. Sites of practice include: § William P. Clements Jr. University Hospital is a state-of-the art facility that is visually appealing, incorporates advanced technology, and was designed for patient comfort and well-being and to enhance multidisciplinary collaboration, Clements... The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center is seeking an outstanding full time Electrophysiologist Cardiologist. The candidate will carry out regular attending duties within the Division of Cardiology, as well as participate in teaching and training of fellows, house staff, and medical students. Candidate will be superior in all aspects of Electrophysiology. Cardiology Division, Facilities & Equipment: Nationally recognized Cardiology Division with more than 100 faculty members that fosters a collegial and collaborative environment with a focus on faculty career development. You will be joining a section of electrophysiology that currently has 5 faculty members that work well in a collegial fashion. Sites of practice include: § William P. Clements Jr. University Hospital is a state-of-the art facility that is visually appealing, incorporates advanced technology, and was designed for patient comfort and well-being and to enhance multidisciplinary collaboration, Clements University Hospital is a centerpiece for carrying out UT Southwestern’s three-part mission – to heal, innovate, and educate. § Parkland Memorial Hospital, Dallas County’s exemplary urban public hospital which provides outstanding diagnosis and treatment for virtually every type of condition or disease. § Clinical Heart and Vascular Center, where ambulatory care at UT Southwestern is delivered in a collaborative manner with our allied health care team. ACGME-accredited Cardiology fellowship programs including Cardiovascular Disease, Clinical Cardiac Electrophysiology, Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant, Interventional Cardiology, as well as Texas Medical Board-accredited fellowship programs in Structural Interventional Cardiology, Advanced Echocardiography, Cardio-Oncology, and Cardiology Advanced Research and Clinical Training, Hypertension. A close collaboration exists with the Department of Cardiovascular and Thoracic Surgery comprised of skilled cardiac surgeons who serve as a regional referral source for complex, quaternary care. Research Environment: Research interests are supported by a culture of collaboration with our strong basic science and clinical teams within the department and across the campus Interdisciplinary care conferences that serve as springboards for clinically relevant research Robust research coaching and mentorship Advanced clinical and pre-clinical instruments and resources Administrative, biostatistical and logistical support resources within the department Applicants should meet these qualifications: Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) or foreign equivalent Successful completion of an ACGME-accredited Cardiology and Electrophysiology fellowship programs Board Certified in Cardiology and subspecialty boarded in Clinical Cardiac Electrophysiology An unrestricted license to practice medicine in Texas UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. T