    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23928850/research-assistant-instructor-internal-medicine-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Instructor - Internal Medicine",
      "description": "Research Assistant Instructor - Internal Medicine job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Research Assistant Instructor - Internal Medicine job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 194191 Research Assistant Instructor – Internal Medicine Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 976294 Category: Faculty and Physicians 23928850 Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases and Geographic Medicine, is seeking a full-time Assistant Instructor. This position will provide expertise, support, and supervision for multiple projects focused on bacterial genomics. Specific scientific areas of expertise include phenotypic testing of bacterial isolates, DNA isolation / sequencing of individuals bacteria as well as polymicrobial bacterial communities (such as the gut microbiome), and genetic manipulation (i.e. gene knockout) of various bacterial strains. The scope of position will include generation of data, management of data output, initial bioinformatic analysis steps, quality control, lab management, and scientific writing, in addition, future responsibilities will include training of junior lab members and students. Requirements: ·       Ph.D. ·       Minimum 3 years of experience. ·       Completion of postdoctoral training. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  