    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23884227/faculty-associate-sports-medicine-orthopaedic-surgery-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "FACULTY ASSOCIATE - Sports Medicine Orthopaedic Surgery",
      "description": "FACULTY ASSOCIATE - Sports Medicine Orthopaedic Surgery job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX FACULTY ASSOCIATE - Sports Medicine Orthopaedic Surgery job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 193715 FACULTY ASSOCIATE – Sports Medicine Orthopaedic Surgery Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 974751 Category: Faculty and Physicians 23884227 Responsibilities The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a Board-Certified/Board-Eligible Orthopaedic Sports Medicine Surgeon to serve as a Team Physician for the Dallas Stars of the National Hockey League (NHL). The Team Physician will provide orthopaedic and musculoskeletal care for Dallas Stars players in collaboration with the organization’s medical, athletic training, and performance teams. Responsibilities will include evaluation and management of injuries, game and team coverage, treatment recommendations, coordination of specialty care, and participation in return-to-play decisions. The physician will hold an academic appointment within the Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at UT Southwestern Medical Center and serve as part of the multidisciplinary team supporting the health, safety, and performance of Dallas Stars athletes. M.D. or D.O. degree from an accredited medical school. Completion of an accredited residency in Orthopaedic Surgery. Minimum of five (5) years of clinical experience as a practicing orthopaedic surgeon. Board certification in Orthopaedic Surgery. Eligible for or currently holds an unrestricted license to practice medicine in the State of Texas. Experience evaluating and treating musculoskeletal injuries, including conditions commonly encountered in competitive or professional athletics. Ability to participate in scheduled team and game coverage and collaborate effectively within a multidisciplinary sports medicine team. CV Required UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensiv