    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/22342311/assistant-professor-of-dermatology-tenure-track-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Dermatology, Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Dermatology, Tenure Track job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Assistant Professor of Dermatology, Tenure Track job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 171672 Assistant Professor of Dermatology, Tenure Track Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 883733 Category: Faculty and Physicians 22342311 Responsibilities The Department of Dermatology invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. We are seeking an academic research dermatologist with expertise in translational science to join our vibrant and growing research community. The successful candidate will be an innovator in skin disease research, developing and applying novel methodologies to address high-impact questions at the interface of basic discovery and clinical translation. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, genetics and genomics of skin disease, cancer, immunology and inflammation, tissue engineering and regenerative biology, computational biology, and advanced imaging or molecular techniques. Candidates will be expected to establish an independent, externally funded research program and to foster multidisciplinary collaborations within the Department of Dermatology and across the broader scientific community at UT Southwestern.  In addition to research, candidates will contribute to the department’s academic mission by mentoring trainees, supporting team science, and advancing knowledge that improves care for patients with skin disease. Why UT Southwestern? Collaborative, collegial environment: UT Southwestern fosters deep collaboration across disciplines, offering unmatched opportunities to partner with clinicians and scientists across the institution. World-class faculty: Home to six Nobel Laureates and distinguished investigators, our campus provides an intellectually rich setting where discovery thrives. Strong funding support: Robust state and institutional funding mechanisms provide additional opportunities for research support, complementing traditional extramural funding sources. Rapid growth: With a steep upward trajectory in both research and clinical programs, UT Southwestern offers fertile ground for building an ambitious and creative career. Excellence in Dermatology: Our Department is nationally recognized for both scientific discovery and clinical excellence, with renowned faculty and a robust clinical trials infrastructure that accelerates translation of discovery into patient care. Commitment to training: A federally funded T32 training program supports the next generation of physician-scientists, ensuring a rich environment for mentorship and career development. This position offers the opportunity to join a leading-edge academic environment with access to exceptional research infrastructure, clinical resources, and a collaborative network of investigators committed to advancing dermatologic science from the bench to the bedside. Education: MD or MD, PhD degree Board Certification: Board certified or eligible in Dermatology Licensure: Eligible for Texas medical licensure Demonstrated clinical excellence in inpatient, outpatient, and/or procedural Dermatology Commitment to the academic mission, including education, mentorship, and scholarly contribution Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively in a multidisciplinary team environment Record of scholarly activity in translational research and program development (commensurate with career stage) Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, a statement of research/vision statement, copies of impactful publications, and contact information for references. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Linkedin Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees Let’s Get Started Join Talent Community Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Previous Next Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. Brenda Edwards Licensed Clinical Social Worker UT Southwestern is a great place to work and learn. Innovation and creativity to improve the quality of patient care are encouraged. Leadership within my team and department is supportive. Denise Anderson Denise Anderson GME Coordinator I I love working at UT Southwestern because of its great staff and great benefits. Everyday is extraordinary because there’s opportunity to expand your knowledge and advance your career. Navigation Home Why Work Here Locations Life in Dallas Benefits Job Search Results Sitemap Departments Advanced Practice Providers Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Residencies & Fellowships Quick Links Patient Care Research Education & Training Newsroom About Us UTSW Corporate Home Address 6001 Forest Park Road Suite NG3.111 Dallas, Texas 75235 Phone 214-648-9810 Annual Security Report (ASR) This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community. As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. © 2024 UT Southwestern Medical Center | All Rights Reserved Opens in a new window Patient Rights Open Records Privacy Policy Site Policies - powered by Enfold-Hodes-Accessible WordPress Theme We use cookies to improve and personalize your experience and to analyze website perf