      "title": "Research Investigator - Pathology",
      "description": "Research Investigator - Pathology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Research Investigator - Pathology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 192279 Research Investigator – Pathology Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 968052 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 23774001 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The Department of Pathology at the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center is seeking an exceptional research investigator at the Assistant Professor level on the Research Track. The candidate should have expertise in neuroscience, immunology, stem cell biology, and cancer biology and will employ state‐of‐the art technologies to investigate the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying human disease. Responsibilities include conducting innovative basic and translational research in support of the laboratory’s research program, collecting and analyzing data, preparing manuscripts for publication, contributing to the development of extramural grant applications, and mentoring graduate students, research technicians, and new postdoctoral fellows.  The Department has an outstanding mix of young, mid‐career and senior investigators who operate in a collegial and stimulating environment. The candidate must possess a PhD and should have a strong publication record in journals of... The Department of Pathology at the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center is seeking an exceptional research investigator at the Assistant Professor level on the Research Track. The candidate should have expertise in neuroscience, immunology, stem cell biology, and cancer biology and will employ state‐of‐the art technologies to investigate the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying human disease. Responsibilities include conducting innovative basic and translational research in support of the laboratory’s research program, collecting and analyzing data, preparing manuscripts for publication, contributing to the development of extramural grant applications, and mentoring graduate students, research technicians, and new postdoctoral fellows.  The Department has an outstanding mix of young, mid‐career and senior investigators who operate in a collegial and stimulating environment. The candidate must possess a PhD and should have a strong publication record in journals of impact. Applicants must complete an online application, attaching a cover letter, curriculum vitae, brief research statement, and contact information for at least three references. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This positio