    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23750498/hematologist-and-medical-oncologist-frisco-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Hematologist and Medical Oncologist - Frisco",
      "description": "Hematologist and Medical Oncologist - Frisco job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Hematologist and Medical Oncologist - Frisco job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 191958 Hematologist and Medical Oncologist – Frisco Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 967526 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 23750498 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a board-certified (or eligible) Hematologist and Medical Oncologist to join our dynamic practice located in Frisco, Texas. This is a unique opportunity for a clinician-educator to deliver high-quality, comprehensive cancer care in a hybrid model that blends academic and community medicine. The selected candidate will support the continued expansion of regional oncology services throughout the DFW area by treating a broad range of hematologic and oncologic conditions in a state-of-the-art facility with on-site infusion, lab, dietitian, and social work support. As part of North Texas’s only NCI-designated cancer center, you will collaborate closely with academic colleagues through tumor boards, research conferences, and shared clinical trials. You will also have protected time to develop a disease-specific interest and the opportunity to educate medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical trial leadership is strongly supported with a dedicated... UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a board-certified (or eligible) Hematologist and Medical Oncologist to join our dynamic practice located in Frisco, Texas. This is a unique opportunity for a clinician-educator to deliver high-quality, comprehensive cancer care in a hybrid model that blends academic and community medicine. The selected candidate will support the continued expansion of regional oncology services throughout the DFW area by treating a broad range of hematologic and oncologic conditions in a state-of-the-art facility with on-site infusion, lab, dietitian, and social work support. As part of North Texas’s only NCI-designated cancer center, you will collaborate closely with academic colleagues through tumor boards, research conferences, and shared clinical trials. You will also have protected time to develop a disease-specific interest and the opportunity to educate medical students, residents, and fellows. Clinical trial leadership is strongly supported with a dedicated full-time research coordinator.  We offer a competitive salary with productivity incentives, full benefits including CME support, malpractice coverage, and 401K. Our division values clinical excellence, innovation, and compassionate care—and we are especially excited to grow our presence in Frisco to meet the needs of patients closer to home. Applicants must have an M.D. degree or equivalent, from an approved LCME medical school, and satisfactory completion of an Internal Medicine residency program from an ACGME accredited program. Candidates must be eligible for Texas medical licensure, be board certified in Internal Medicine and board certified/eligible in Hematology Oncology. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook (Opens in a new window) Share on Twitter (Opens in a new window) Share on Linkedin (Opens in a new window) Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees (Opens in a new window) Let’s Get Started Thank you for filling out the form. First Name * Last Name * Email * City City entered successfuly State State entered successfuly Country Country entered successfuly Area of Interest Area of Interest entered successfuly Administrative/Clerical Advanced Practice Provider Allied Health Campus Services Clinical Faculty and Physicians Finance Hospital Based Nurses Housekeeping Information Technology Insurance/Billing Nurse Educators Nursing Nutrition Professional & Executive Research & Laboratory Skilled Trade/Facilities Mgmt. Yes, I agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy * No, I do not wish to be contacted with marketing and job alerts from UT Southwestern Medical Center. Remember Me Continue to Apply © 2026 Symphony Talent Terms of Use | Privacy Join Talent Community (Opens in a new window) Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. Brenda Edwards Licensed Clinical Social Worker UT Southwestern is a great place to work and learn. Innovation and creativity to improve the quality of patient care are encouraged. Leadership within my team and department is supportive. Denise Anderson Denise Anderson GME Coordinator I I love working at UT Southwestern because of its great staff and great benefits. Everyday is extraordinary because there’s opportunity to expand your knowledge and advance your career. Previous Next 1 2 (Opens in a new window) (Opens in a new window) (Opens in a new window) (Opens in a new window) (Opens in a new window) Navigation Home Why Work Here Locations Life in Dallas Benefits Job Search Results Sitemap Departments Advanced Practice Providers Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Residencies & Fellowships Quick Links Patient Care (Opens in a new window) Research (Opens in a new window) Education & Training (Opens in a new window) Newsroom (Opens in a new window) About Us (Opens in a new window) UTSW Corporat