    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23689372/clinical-physician-urology-urps-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Clinical Physician - Urology (URPS)",
      "description": "Clinical Physician - Urology (URPS) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Clinical Physician - Urology (URPS) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 190977 Clinical Physician – Urology (URPS) Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 964828 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 23689372 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities UT Southwestern Medical Center | Dallas/Fort Worth, TX UT Southwestern Medical Center is the No. 1 hospital in Dallas-Fort Worth for the ninth consecutive year and ranks among the nation’s top hospitals for care in 12 specialties – the most in Texas, according to U.S. News & World Report . Our Department of Urology is proud to be recognized as one of the nation’s top 25 hospitals for urologic care with a distinguished team of health care providers devoted to the diagnosis and treatment of urologic conditions. Job Summary UT Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Urology , is seeking a full-time physician to develop a practice in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) to join their state-of-the-art practice in Dallas and Fort Worth. This role offers the opportunity to provide comprehensive urologic care to a diverse patient population and multidisciplinary collaboration. The ideal candidate will demonstrate clinical excellence, a patient-centered approach,... UT Southwestern Medical Center | Dallas/Fort Worth, TX UT Southwestern Medical Center is the No. 1 hospital in Dallas-Fort Worth for the ninth consecutive year and ranks among the nation’s top hospitals for care in 12 specialties – the most in Texas, according to U.S. News & World Report . Our Department of Urology is proud to be recognized as one of the nation’s top 25 hospitals for urologic care with a distinguished team of health care providers devoted to the diagnosis and treatment of urologic conditions. Job Summary UT Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Urology , is seeking a full-time physician to develop a practice in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) to join their state-of-the-art practice in Dallas and Fort Worth. This role offers the opportunity to provide comprehensive urologic care to a diverse patient population and multidisciplinary collaboration. The ideal candidate will demonstrate clinical excellence, a patient-centered approach, and enthusiasm for contributing to an academic medical center committed to innovation, education, and outstanding outcomes. Position Highlights Focused on Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) Mi x of outpatient clinics, inpatient consults, and surgical cases Surgical Cases at Clements University Hospital and John Peter Smith Hospital Access to advanced surgical technologies, including robotics and minimally invasive platforms Works closely with the Urology Residency Program for teaching and mentoring Join a nationally recognized Department of Urology with subspecialty experts and a strong referral base Multidisciplinary collaboration with oncology, radiology, gastroenterology, and primary care teams Compensation & Benefits Competitive rank and base salary commensurate with experience and an outstanding benefit package Allowance for educational and academic pursuits (society dues, books, travel to meetings, license renewal) Relocation assistance available Two types of retirement programs, including a lifetime annuity pension plan with a substantial employer match contribution About Dallas/Fort Worth, TX The Dallas area boasts a low cost of living with diverse neighborhoods. The area has world-class quality of life options, with more than 175 museums and art galleries, premier performance halls, numerous parks, lakes, golf courses and seven professional sport franchises. With top-rated schools, vibrant dining and entertainment options, and a family-friendly atmosphere, Dallas/Fort Worth blends modern amenities with a strong sense of community. Physicians who join UT Southwestern enjoy the opportunity to practice in a state-of-the-art facility while living and working in one of the most dynamic and thriving areas of North Texas. MD or DO degree from an accredited institution Completion of an ACGME-accredited Urology residency Board-Certified/Board-Eligible General Urologist Eligible for Texas medical licensure Strong commitment to clinical excellence, education, and multidisciplinary collaboration. Catherine Albert Administrative Manager, Department of Urology UT Southwestern Medical Center P: 972-648-0021 Email: catherine.albert@UTSouthwestern.edu UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook (Opens in a new window) Share on Twitter (Opens in a new window) Share on Linkedin (Opens in a new window) Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees (Opens in a new window) Let’s Get Started Thank you for filling out the form. First Name * Last Name * Email * City City entered successfuly State State entered successfuly Country Country entered successfuly Area of Interest Area of Interest entered successfuly Administrative/Clerical Advanced Practice Provider Allied Health Campus Services Clinical Faculty and Physicians Finance Hospital Based Nurses Housekeeping Information Technology Insurance/Billing Nurse Educators Nursing Nutrition Professional & Executive Research & Laboratory Skilled Trade/Facilities Mgmt. Yes, I agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy * No, I do not wish to be contacted with marketing and job alerts from UT Southwestern Medical Center. Remember Me Continue to Apply © 2026 Symphony Talent Terms of Use | Privacy Join Talent Community (Opens in a new window) Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor 