    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23245935/pediatric-hepatologist-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Pediatric Hepatologist",
      "description": "Pediatric Hepatologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Pediatric Hepatologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 184412 Pediatric Hepatologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 935994 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 23245935 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Pediatrics is seeking an outstanding pediatric hepatologist to join the Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition at UT Southwestern and Children’s Health Dallas.  Our Hepatology team currently consists of 7 CAQ Hepatologists and is supported by a dedicated inpatient team of APPs offering 24/7/365 coverage for our pediatric patients.  Liver transplant volume is expected to range from 15-25 transplants in 2026.  The team benefits from close relationships with in-house Pediatric ERCP and EUS experts as well as Interventional Radiology and other supporting specialties. The physician in this position is expected to care for patients with a wide range of liver disorders, including pre- and post-liver transplant patients. Excellence in the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, along with a desire to become a leader in the field is expected. Applicants must be eligible for medical... The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Pediatrics is seeking an outstanding pediatric hepatologist to join the Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Nutrition at UT Southwestern and Children’s Health Dallas.  Our Hepatology team currently consists of 7 CAQ Hepatologists and is supported by a dedicated inpatient team of APPs offering 24/7/365 coverage for our pediatric patients.  Liver transplant volume is expected to range from 15-25 transplants in 2026.  The team benefits from close relationships with in-house Pediatric ERCP and EUS experts as well as Interventional Radiology and other supporting specialties. The physician in this position is expected to care for patients with a wide range of liver disorders, including pre- and post-liver transplant patients. Excellence in the teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, along with a desire to become a leader in the field is expected. Applicants must be eligible for medical licensure in the state of Texas and be board eligible or certified in Pediatric Gastroenterology as well as Hepatology. Potential candidates should apply online at https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ (search for Job #935994) and upload a curriculum vitae and a letter of interest. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook (Opens in a new window) Share on Twitter (Opens in a new window) Share on Linkedin (Opens in a new window) Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees (Opens in a new window) Let’s Get Started Thank you for filling out the form. First Name * Last Name * Email * City City entered successfuly State State entered successfuly Country Country entered successfuly Area of Interest Area of Interest entered successfuly Administrative/Clerical Advanced Practice Provider Allied Health Campus Services Clinical Faculty and Physicians Finance Hospital Based Nurses Housekeeping Information Technology Insurance/Billing Nurse Educators Nursing Nutrition Professional & Executive Research & Laboratory Skilled Trade/Facilities Mgmt. Yes, I agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy * No, I do not wish to be contacted with marketing and job alerts from UT Southwestern Medical Center. Remember Me Continue to Apply © 2026 Symphony Talent Terms of Use | Privacy Join Talent Community (Opens in a new window) Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Fa