    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23179435/clinical-assistant-professor-hospitalist-hybrid-days-nights-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor Hospitalist (Hybrid – Days/Nights)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor Hospitalist (Hybrid – Days/Nights)  job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Clinical Assistant Professor Hospitalist (Hybrid – Days/Nights)  job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 183604 Clinical Assistant Professor Hospitalist (Hybrid – Days/Nights) Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 933755 Category: Faculty and Physicians 23179435 Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center Department of Internal Medicine is recruiting Academic Hospitalists to join the Division of Hospital Medicine at the rank of Assistant Professor. This is a full-time position featuring a hybrid schedule of 50%-day shifts and 50%-night shifts, providing a unique opportunity to engage in diverse clinical experiences at one of the nation’s leading academic institutions. Our hospitalists provide direct patient care while playing a critical role in teaching and mentoring the next generation of physicians, including residents and medical students. UT Southwestern Medical Center is the No.1 hospital in Dallas Fort-Worth for the eighth consecutive year and ranks among the nation’s top hospitals for care in 11 specialties – the most of any hospital in Texas, according to the U.S. News & World Report. Key Responsibilities: ·       Provide exceptional clinical care to a high-complexity patient population on med-surg level units ·       Day shifts: rounding on general ward patients or admitting new patients ·       Night shifts: o    Primarily admitting hospital medicine patients and patients on behalf of other medical services at night ·       Teach and mentor internal medicine residents and medical students while on teaching services ·       Collaborate with advanced practice providers in a shared visit model during some weeks ·       No procedures and closed ICU’s Scheduling: ·       7 days on/7 days off, with 12-hour shifts ·       175 shifts per year ·       Alternate between days and nights every 4 weeks ·       Day shifts: Mostly 12-hour shifts (no overnight pager call) ·       Night shifts: Staggered shifts, Guarantee of either Thanksgiving Day or Christmas Day off every year (usually alternating years) Qualifications: ·       MD or DO degree, or foreign equivalent, from an accredited institution ·       Board certified or board eligible with the American Board of Internal Medicine ·       Unrestricted Texas medical licensure ·       Commitment to participation in quality improvement, patient safety initiatives, and other scholarly activities If interested, please submit a copy of your current CV and best contact information. All inquiries and personal information are kept confidential. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Linkedin Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees Let’s Get Started Join Talent Community Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Previous Next Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. Brenda Edwards Licensed Clinical Social Worker UT Southwestern is a great place to work and learn. Innovation and creativity to improve the quality of patient care are encouraged. Leadership within my team and department is supportive. Denise Anderson Denise Anderson GME Coordinator I I love working at UT Southwestern because of its great staff and great benefits. Everyday is extraordinary because there’s opportunity to expand your knowledge and advance your career. Navigation Home Why Work Here Locations Life in Dallas Benefits Job Search Results Sitemap Departments Advanced Practice Providers Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Residencies & Fellowships Quick Links Patient Care Research Education & Training Newsroom About Us UTSW Corporate Home Address 6001 Forest Park Road