      "description": "Neuro-Oncologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Neuro-Oncologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 182431 Neuro-Oncologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 929208 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 23096287 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Neurology, is seeking a faculty member with a focused clinical and research interest in Neuro-Oncology.  UT Southwestern is recognized for offering an exceptional level of expertise in Neuro-Oncology, providing effective treatment options based on the latest research and the highest standards of care. The Neuro-Oncology Program at UT Southwestern is a growing, high-volume service line that aims to provide patients with robust, multidisciplinary care.  We have active basic, translational, and clinical research programs.  There is excellent collaboration between Neuro-Oncology, Neurosurgery, Radiation Oncology, PM&R, Neuropathology, and 