    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23094362/clinical-assistant-professor-tumor-group-neurological-surgery-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Tumor Group Neurological Surgery",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Tumor Group Neurological Surgery job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Clinical Assistant Professor - Tumor Group Neurological Surgery job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 182576 Clinical Assistant Professor – Tumor Group Neurological Surgery Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 927510 Category: Faculty and Physicians 23094362 Responsibilities This individual would build a clinical neurosurgery practice focusing on neuro-oncological surgery, including both routine and complex surgeries.  This position will provide clinical services at two primary inpatient locations: Parkland Health & Hospital System and Clements University Hospital, as well as ambulatory clinics across the DFW region, including the Simmons Comprehensive Cancer Center on the main campus, Frisco, or Ft Worth.  In support of the Department’s academic mission, faculty members are expected to teach neurosurgery residents and medical students; develop an area of academic focus and participate in clinical research activities. It is strongly preferred that the candidate will have a tumor fellowship. Candidates must be board certified or eligible in Neurosurgery and eligible for a Texas Medical License. Interested and qualified surgeons should apply online and upload a cover letter and curriculum vitae. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As