    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/23083899/epilepsy-faculty-early-career-investigator-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Epilepsy Faculty - Early Career Investigator",
      "description": "Epilepsy Faculty - Early Career Investigator job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Epilepsy Faculty - Early Career Investigator job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 181783 Epilepsy Faculty – Early Career Investigator Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 926402 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 23083899 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The Department of Neurology at UT Southwestern School of Medicine is seeking a research faculty member who will establish and maintain an independent, externally funded laboratory focused on basic and/or translational research in epilepsy and related neurodevelopmental or neurological disorders.  Responsibilities include designing and executing rigorous experimental studies; developing innovative research programs aligned with institutional priorities; publishing findings in peer-reviewed journals; and presenting research at national and international scientific meetings.  The faculty member will ensure compliance with all institutional, federal, and ethical regulations governing laboratory research, including animal and biosafety protocols, and will oversee laboratory operations, budgeting, and personnel managment. Additionally, the successful candidate will contribute to the academic mission through mentorship and training of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and research... The Department of Neurology at UT Southwestern School of Medicine is seeking a research faculty member who will establish and maintain an independent, externally funded laboratory focused on basic and/or translational research in epilepsy and related neurodevelopmental or neurological disorders.  Responsibilities include designing and executing rigorous experimental studies; developing innovative research programs aligned with institutional priorities; publishing findings in peer-reviewed journals; and presenting research at national and international scientific meetings.  The faculty member will ensure compliance with all institutional, federal, and ethical regulations governing laboratory research, including animal and biosafety protocols, and will oversee laboratory operations, budgeting, and personnel managment. Additionally, the successful candidate will contribute to the academic mission through mentorship and training of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and research staff, and may participate in teaching activities appropriatee to their expertise.  Service responsibilities include participation in departmental, institutional, and professional committees, as well as engagement in collaborative research initiatives.  The successful candidate is expected to foster a collaborative, inclusive research environment and to contribute to the advancement of epilepsy research through interdisciplinary partnerships. Qualifications: -PhD, MD, or MD/PhD trained -Significant post-doctoral fellowship training -Track record that indicates a readiness for independent career UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tu