      "description": "Genitourinary Clinical Radiation Oncologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Genitourinary Clinical Radiation Oncologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 180860 Genitourinary Clinical Radiation Oncologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 922008 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 22933166 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The Department of Radiation Oncology at UT Southwestern is looking for a radiation oncologist to join our genitourinary disease-oriented team. Qualification Experience with brachytherapy, prostate fiducial, and peri-rectal Hydrogel spacerplacement is encouraged. M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree from an ACGME-approved medical school or equivalent and completion of a radiation oncology residency program from an approved institution. Board certification or eligibility in Radiation Oncology and eligibility for Texas medical licensure. Interest in initiating new clinical trials and adaptive radiotherapy strategies, as well as collabo