    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/22917574/division-chief-obstetric-anesthesiology-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Division Chief - Obstetric Anesthesiology",
      "description": "Division Chief - Obstetric Anesthesiology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Division Chief - Obstetric Anesthesiology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 180627 Division Chief – Obstetric Anesthesiology Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 920775 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 22917574 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities Our Division of Obstetric Anesthesiology is one of the nation’s busiest and leading sites, overseeing deliveries at both Parkland Hospital and Clements University Hospital. Parkland Hospital is among the nation’s highest-volume obstetric centers, with approximately 13,000 deliveries annually and a 32% cesarean section rate; it serves as a safety net hospital caring for some of the highest-risk pregnancies in Texas. William P. Clements Jr. University Hospital manages approximately 2,000 complex deliveries annually, many involving patients with significant medical comorbidities. The Department of Anesthesiology and Pain Management at UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a Division Chief of Obstetric Anesthesiology to lead our efforts in treatment and care of the obstetric patient population. This individual will provide strategic, clinical, and academic leadership for UT Southwestern’s obstetric anesthesia services. This individual will oversee high-volume, high-acuity clinical operations,... Our Division of Obstetric Anesthesiology is one of the nation’s busiest and leading sites, overseeing deliveries at both Parkland Hospital and Clements University Hospital. Parkland Hospital is among the nation’s highest-volume obstetric centers, with approximately 13,000 deliveries annually and a 32% cesarean section rate; it serves as a safety net hospital caring for some of the highest-risk pregnancies in Texas. William P. Clements Jr. University Hospital manages approximately 2,000 complex deliveries annually, many involving patients with significant medical comorbidities. The Department of Anesthesiology and Pain Management at UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a Division Chief of Obstetric Anesthesiology to lead our efforts in treatment and care of the obstetric patient population. This individual will provide strategic, clinical, and academic leadership for UT Southwestern’s obstetric anesthesia services. This individual will oversee high-volume, high-acuity clinical operations, support faculty and trainee development. The Division Chief will lead our partnership with Obstetrics & Gynecology leadership across both hospitals as well as multidisciplinary collaboration in clinical, research, and educational missions. The Division provides dedicated 24/7 in-house obstetric anesthesia coverage at both facilities and plays a central role in resident and fellow education. Position Highlights Provide strategic, clinical, and academic leadership for the Division of Obstetric Anesthesiology across two major academic hospitals and in alignment with departmental and institutional priorities Oversee high-volume, high-acuity obstetric anesthesia services, including 24/7 coverage, staffing models, and standardized clinical pathway Ensure excellence in patient safety, quality, efficiency, and patient-centered care across all practice sites Serve as the Division and Department representative at obstetric operational meetings at both clinical sites and collaborate closely with the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology and institutional leadership Lead faculty recruitment, development, evaluation, and performance management, including oversight of Annual Professional Reviews. Foster a culture of scholarly inquiry, quality improvement, and innovation, supporting clinical research and national academic engagement Direct faculty staffing models, scheduling, and resource utilization Maintain an active clinical practice while balancing significant leadership and academic responsibilities Lead and mentor faculty, residents, fellows, CRNAs, and advanced practice providers Support and expand resident and fellowship education, including oversight of two ACGME-accredited OB Anesthesia fellowship position Utilize a MOCA-certified simulation center for multidisciplinary and team-based training Foster and support clinical and translational research within obstetric anesthesiology IDEAL EXPERIENCE Academic record consistent with the rank of Associate Professor or higher. Expertise in obstetric anesthesia, including high-risk parturients with complex medical, cardiac and obstetric comorbidities Accomplished obstetric anesthesiologist with a strong record of high-quality clinical outcomes and commitment to patient-centered care Effective leader who fosters an environment of professionalism, accountability, and continuous improvement within an academic center, while emphasizing mentorship, education, and multidisciplinary collaboration Comfortable working within the labor and delivery structure, partnering with clinical and administrative leaders to support division growth Opportunity to shape and direct the future of Obstetric Anesthesiology through strategic planning, faculty recruitment, research, quality improvement, clinical and scholarly activities M.D. or D.O. degree from an accredited institution Completion of an ACGME-accredited Anesthesiology residency Fellowship training in Obstetric Anesthesiology Board-Certified by the American Board of Anesthesiology Eligible for Texas medical licensure Strong commitment to clinical excellence, education, research, and multidisciplinary collaboration Contact: Dustin Floyd. M.B.A. Clinical Physician Recruiter, Talent Acquisition Office of Human Resources UT Southwestern Medical Center P: 972-573-3895 Email: dustin.floyd@utsouthwestern.edu UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook (Opens 