      "description": "OB/GYN Clinical Physician – Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery (MIGS) and Gynecology (Fort Worth, Texas) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Fort Worth, TX OB/GYN Clinical Physician – Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery (MIGS) and Gynecology (Fort Worth, Texas) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Fort Worth, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 180521 OB/GYN Clinical Physician – Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery (MIGS) and Gynecology (Fort Worth, Texas) Location: Fort Worth , TX Location Type: Job Number: 920347 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 22911798 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities UT Southwestern is the No. 1 hospital in Dallas-Fort Worth and ranks among the top 50 hospitals nationally in 12 specialties ranging from brain to heart to cancer care – the most of any hospital in Texas, according to U.S. News & World Report’s annual Best Hospitals rankings in the 2025 report, nine of our specialties ranked in the top 25 in the nation. Job Summary:  The ideal candidate will be a highly motivated individual with strong leadership and communication skills. The ideal candidate should have demonstrated excellence in clinical care, an academic track record performing or participating in scholarly activity, and a commitment to the education and development of colleagues and trainees. The successful candidate will join a dynamic division of Gynecologists in an ambulatory University-based practice setting. The principle clinical assignment will be to provide Gynecologic clinical care to complex gynecologic patients with multi-disciplinary programs in endometriosis,... UT Southwestern is the No. 1 hospital in Dallas-Fort Worth and ranks among the top 50 hospitals nationally in 12 specialties ranging from brain to heart to cancer care – the most of any hospital in Texas, according to U.S. News & World Report’s annual Best Hospitals rankings in the 2025 report, nine of our specialties ranked in the top 25 in the nation. Job Summary:  The ideal candidate will be a highly motivated individual with strong leadership and communication skills. The ideal candidate should have demonstrated excellence in clinical care, an academic track record performing or participating in scholarly activity, and a commitment to the education and development of colleagues and trainees. The successful candidate will join a dynamic division of Gynecologists in an ambulatory University-based practice setting. The principle clinical assignment will be to provide Gynecologic clinical care to complex gynecologic patients with multi-disciplinary programs in endometriosis, fibroid care, and pelvic pain. Position Highlights: Engagement in resident and medical student education, as well as clinical or scholarly activities that advance the field of Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery & Gynecology Benefits: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Two types of retirement programs, including a lifetime annuity pension plan with a substantial employer match contribution Fort Worth, Texas: Fort Worth is now the 11th largest city in the U.S. after recently surpassing Austin. The city offers an exceptional lifestyle with a vibrant cultural scene highlighted by the renowned Kimbell Art Museum, Modern Art Museum, and Amon Carter Museum in the Cultural District. The city is a sports hub, home to Texas Motor Speedway and Dickies Arena, with convenient access to Dallas Cowboys and Texas Rangers venues nearby. Residents enjoy iconic steakhouses, award-winning BBQ, Tex-Mex, craft breweries, and an expanding selection of chef-driven restaurants. Fort Worth’s rich Western heritage comes to life in the Stockyards, daily cattle drives, and annual festivals. With no state income tax, a cost of living approximately 4% below the national average, and a wide selection of affordable, family-friendly neighborhoods and top-rated schools, the city provides an outstanding quality of life for professionals and families alike. MD or DO degree from an accredited institution Completion of an ACGME-accredited residency in obstetrics and gynecology Completion of an AAGL approved Fellowship in Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery, or equivalent experience, is preferred Have attained or be eligible for Texas medical licensure and board certification by the American Board of Obstetrics & Gynecology Strong commitment to clinical excellence, education, and multidisciplinary collaboration Interested candidates should apply online at https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ (Job# 920347) and upload a curriculum vitae, letter of interest and contact information for references. Contact: Megan Davis Clinical Physician Recruiter, Talent Acquisition Office of Human Resources UT Southwestern Medical Center P: 972-449-9836 Email: megan.davis@utsouthwestern.edu UT Sout