      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - General Otolaryngology",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor - General Otolaryngology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Fort Worth, TX Clinical Assistant Professor - General Otolaryngology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Fort Worth, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 180278 Clinical Assistant Professor – General Otolaryngology Location: Fort Worth , TX Location Type: Job Number: 919109 Category: Faculty and Physicians 22896864 Responsibilities UT Southwestern Medical Center is the No. 1 hospital in Dallas-Fort Worth and ranks among the top 50 hospitals nationally in 12 specialties ranging from brain to heart to cancer care – the most of any hospital in Texas, according to U.S. News & World Report’s annual Best Hospitals rankings in the 2025 report, nine of our specialties ranked in the top 25 in the nation. Job Summary The Department of Otolaryngology – Head and Neck Surgery at UT Southwestern Medical Center is actively recruiting qualified candidates for a faculty position in Otolaryngology. The successful candidate will maintain a busy ambulatory otolaryngology practice, with a focus on general ENT care, at the UT Southwestern Monty and Tex Moncrief Medical Center, located on the Fort Worth campus. Position Highlights · Integrate evidence-based medicine and current clinical guidelines into patient care and teaching. · Collaborate in multidisciplinary teams with related subspecialties (e.g., neurotology, head and neck oncology, speech pathology, and communication and vestibular disorders). · Engagement with colleagues and residents at monthly grand rounds, as well as clinical and scholarly activities that advance the field of otolaryngology. Fort Worth, Texas Fort Worth is now the 11th largest city in the U.S. after recently surpassing Austin. The city offers an exceptional lifestyle with a vibrant cultural scene highlighted by the renowned Kimbell Art Museum, Modern Art Museum, and Amon Carter Museum in the Cultural District. The city is a sports hub, home to Texas Motor Speedway and Dickies Arena, with convenient access to Dallas Cowboys and Texas Rangers venues nearby. Residents enjoy iconic steakhouses, award-winning BBQ, Tex-Mex, craft breweries, and an expanding selection of chef-driven restaurants. Fort Worth’s rich Western heritage comes to life in the Stockyards, daily cattle drives, and annual festivals. With no state income tax, a cost of living approximately 4% below the national average, and a wide selection of affordable, family-friendly neighborhoods and top-rated schools, the city provides an outstanding quality of life for professionals and families alike. Individuals applying for this position must have the following qualifications: MD or DO degree from an accredited institution Completion of an ACGME-accredited residency Board Certified in Otolaryngology Eligible for Texas medical licensure Strong commitment to clinical excellence, education, and multidisciplinary collaboration. All interested candidates should apply online at Careers at University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center (utsouthwestern.edu) . UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is s