    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/22874610/instructor-bioinformatics-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Instructor - Bioinformatics",
      "description": "Instructor - Bioinformatics job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Instructor - Bioinformatics job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 167586 Instructor – Bioinformatics Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 864909 Category: Faculty and Physicians 22874610 Responsibilities The Lyda Hill Department of Bioinformatics at the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center is looking to hire a faculty position at the level of an Instructor. Candidates must possses a Ph.D. and postdoctoral training Job duties as Instructor include: Organize weekly “rapid fire” paper review in lab meeting where we select the articles we read and present in the weekly journal club In the wet-lab part of our group, train technicians, graduate students and postdocs in molecular cell biology. This includes instructions in current and novel protocols and techniques and help them setting up new assays and validate them Bi-weekly subgroup meetings on cell and molecular biology run tutorials on novel technologies in the field of mocular biology, biochemistry and in particular all flavors of genome engineering and screening technologies Organize seminars with field scientist who support our wet-lab equipment. Keep up to date with new technology development and helps train our students and postdocs on these instruments UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal o