      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Dermatology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Clinical Assistant Professor - Dermatology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 174208 Clinical Assistant Professor – Dermatology Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 895228 Category: Faculty and Physicians 22452713 Responsibilities UT Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Dermatology, is seeking a Board-Certified or Board-Eligible Dermatologist to join our dynamic and growing faculty as a Clinical Assistant Professor. Duties will include providing excellent patient care for eight (8) ½ days each week at our main camps Dermatology clinic. Our department is nationally recognized and deeply engaged in advancing the field of dermatology through high-quality patient care, innovative education, and scholarly activity. We are committed to cultivating an environment where faculty thrive as clinicians, educators, and collaborators. Position Highlights: Robust and diverse clinical practice across general and subspecialty dermatology Opportunities to develop focused areas of clinical interest Flexible scheduling options, including consideration for less than full-time appointments Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources within a leading academic medical center Qualifications M.D. or M.D./Ph.D degree with board certification or eligibility in Dermatology Eligibility for an unrestricted medical license in the State of Texas Demonstrated commitment to academic medicine and team-based care Potential candidates should apply online at https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ and upload a curriculum vitae. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Linkedin Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees Let’s Get Started Join Talent Community Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Previous Next Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. Brenda Edwards Licensed Clinical Social Worker UT Southwestern is a great place to work and learn. Innovation and creativity to improve the quality of patient care are encouraged. Leadership within my team and department is supportive. Denise Anderson Denise Anderson GME Coordinator I I love working at UT Southwestern because of its great staff and great benefits. Everyday is extraordinary because there’s opportunity to expand your knowledge and advance your career. Navigation Home Why Work Here Locations Life in Dallas Benefits Job Search Results Sitemap Departments Advanced Practice Providers Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Residencies & Fellowships Quick Links Patient Care Research Education & Training Newsroom About Us UTSW Corporate Home Address 6001 Forest Park Road Suite NG3.111 Dallas, Texas 75235 Phone 214-648-9810 Annual Security Report (ASR) This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community. As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. © 2024 UT Southwestern Medical Center | All Rights Reserved Opens in a new window Patient Rights Open Records Privacy Policy Site Policies - powered by Enfold-Hodes-Accessible WordPress Theme We use cookies to improve and personalize your experience and to analyze website performance and traffic. Please see our Cookie Policy for a description of how we use cookies or to manage your settings. Accept Scroll to top"
