      "title": "Pediatric Gastroenterologist",
      "description": "Pediatric Gastroenterologist  job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Pediatric Gastroenterologist  job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 170926 Pediatric Gastroenterologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 880654 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 22243070 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Pediatrics, is seeking an outstanding academic pediatric gastroenterologist with interest and expertise in the diagnosis and treatment of motility disorders to join the Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology. The physician in this position is expected to care for patients with the entire spectrum of gastrointestinal motility disorders, as well as disorders of gut-brain interaction and those resulting from congenital disease such as Hirschsprung and imperforate anus.  Collegial and collaborative multidisciplinary programs are currently active in these disorders.  An interest in team science/clinical research is preferred, and excellence in teaching of medical students, residents and fellows is expected. Applicants must be eligible for medical licensure in the state of Texas and be board eligible or certified in Pediatric Gastroenterology. Potential candidates should apply online and upload a curriculum vitae... The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Pediatrics, is seeking an outstanding academic pediatric gastroenterologist with interest and expertise in the diagnosis and treatment of motility disorders to join the Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology. The physician in this position is expected to care for patients with the entire spectrum of gastrointestinal motility disorders, as well as disorders of gut-brain interaction and those resulting from congenital disease such as Hirschsprung and imperforate anus.  Collegial and collaborative multidisciplinary programs are currently active in these disorders.  An interest in team science/clinical research is preferred, and excellence in teaching of medical students, residents and fellows is expected. Applicants must be eligible for medical licensure in the state of Texas and be board eligible or certified in Pediatric Gastroenterology. Potential candidates should apply online and upload a curriculum vitae and a letter of interest. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class pa