    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/21898903/division-director-of-pediatric-dermatology-at-children-s-health-dallas-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Division Director of Pediatric Dermatology at Children’s Health Dallas",
      "description": "Division Director of Pediatric Dermatology at Children’s Health Dallas  job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Division Director of Pediatric Dermatology at Children’s Health Dallas  job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 166719 Division Director of Pediatric Dermatology at Children’s Health Dallas Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 861497 Category: Faculty and Physicians 21898903 Responsibilities The Department of Dermatology at UT Southwestern Medical Center in partnership with Children’s Health Dallas are seeking an accomplished and visionary academic dermatologist. The qualified candidate will serve as Division Director of Pediatric Dermatology at Children’s Health Dallas and lead the development of an academic Division of Pediatric Dermatology at UT Southwestern. Once the division is established will serve as the inaugural, founding UTSW Chief of Pediatric Dermatology. This individual will lead efforts to build a robust, innovative, and sustainable pediatric dermatology program that meets the diverse and growing needs of children and families throughout the Dallas-Fort Worth Metroplex and the surrounding North Texas region. This position will be provided the resources needed to support an ambitious and forward-looking vision aimed at building a nationally recognized program of excellence. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to shape the future of pediatric dermatology at UT Southwestern and Children’s Health Dallas by advancing excellence in clinical care, education, and research, while fostering a collaborative environment for faculty, trainees, and staff. Key Responsibilities: Lead the development and growth of a comprehensive pediatric dermatology program at UT Southwestern and Children’s Health Dallas. Provide strategic direction and oversight for clinical services, ensuring delivery of high-quality, accessible, and patient-centered care. Recruit, mentor, and retain exceptional faculty in partnership with the Chair of Dermatology. Collaborate with institutional partners, including Children’s Health Dallas, to expand clinical services. Champion educational efforts, including training of residents, fellows, and medical students. Advance research and scholarship in pediatric dermatology, with support for faculty and trainees pursuing academic projects. MD or MD/PhD (or equivalent) from an accredited medical school is required. Board certification in Dermatology and Pediatric Dermatology. Must qualify for an unrestricted Texas medical license. Demonstrated record of leadership, program development, and mentorship in an academic setting. Interested candidates should submit a CV via application portal. Please reach out to Jami Armbrester-Harrison, Department Administrator, with questions. Jami.Armbrester@UTSouthwestern.edu UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical ed