      "title": "Nephrologist",
      "description": "Nephrologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Nephrologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 165911 Nephrologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 857723 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 21825161 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Nephrology is seeking a Nephrologist physician scientist.  Position will develop independent and externally funded, as well as collaborative research programs focusing on Cardio-Renal Syndrome. Duties will also include general nephrology and care of dialysis patients, in addition to the teaching and training of medical students, graduate students, house staff, and fellows. Applicants must have an M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree or equivalent, from an approved LCME medical school and satisfactory completion of an Internal Medicine residency and nephrology fellowship from an ACGME accredited program as well as 2 to 5 years o