    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/21679499/professor-and-division-chief-pediatric-urology-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Professor and Division Chief - Pediatric Urology",
      "description": "Professor and Division Chief - Pediatric Urology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Professor and Division Chief - Pediatric Urology job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 163976 Professor and Division Chief – Pediatric Urology Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 849706 Category: Faculty and Physicians 21679499 Responsibilities UT Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Urology, is seeking a full-time physician to serve in the role of Division Chief for Pediatric Urology. This position will be appointed by The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center and Children’s Health with reporting structure to the Department of Urology Chairman at The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center.  The Division Chief of Pediatric Urology shall serve as the leader of his/her respective business unit in addition to fulfilling all clinical, research, and academic programmatic goals as set forth in the letter of employment and other related documents. The Division Chief of Pediatric Urology is dually responsible for achieving programmatic excellence as a senior faculty leader as well as maintaining financial viability of the business unit under the direction of the Chairman. The selected candidate will work with a highly specialized group of physicians and healthcare staff providing comprehensive, multidisciplinary, Urological care. Responsibilities will include both inpatient and outpatient Urology clinical care at training institutions affiliated with UT Southwestern and at UT Southwestern Medical Center clinics and hospitals. Qualifications: Medical degree (M.D. or D.O.) from an accredited institution American Board of Urology certification in Urology with sub-specialty certification in Pediatric Urology Experience: Previous leadership or management experience in a healthcare setting preferred and a minimum of 5 years of clinical experience For consideration, please submit a cover letter and curriculum vitae to: Catherine Albert Administrative Manager, Department of Urology UT Southwestern Medical Center 5323 Harry Hines Blvd. Dallas, TX  75390-9110 Fax:  214-648-4789 catherine.albert@utsouthwestern.edu https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Linkedin Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees Let’s Get Started Join Talent Community Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Previous Next Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. Brenda Edwards Licensed Clinical Social Worker UT Southwestern is a great place to work and learn. Innovation and creativity to improve the quality of patient care are encouraged. Leadership within my team and department is supportive. Denise Anderson Denise Anderson GME Coordinator I I love working at UT Southwestern because of its great staff and great benefits. Everyday is extraordinary because there’s opportunity to expand your knowledge and advance your career. Navigation Home Why Work Here Locations Life in Dallas Benefits Job Search Results Sitemap Departments Advanced Practice Providers Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Residencies & Fellowships Quick Links Patient Care Research Education & Training Newsroom About Us UTSW Corporate Home Address 6001 Forest Park Road Suite NG3.111 Dallas, Texas 75235 Phone 214-648-9810 Annual Security Report (ASR) This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community. As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. © 2024 UT Southwestern Medical Center | All Rights Reserved Opens in a new window Patient Rights Open Records Privacy Policy Site Policies - powered by Enfold-Hodes-Accessible WordPress Theme We use cookies to improve and personalize your experience and to analyze website performance and traffic. Please see our Cookie Policy for a description of how we use cookies or to manage your settings. Accept Scroll to top"
