    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/21633948/pediatric-allergy-immunology-specialist-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Pediatric Allergy & Immunology Specialist",
      "description": "Pediatric Allergy & Immunology Specialist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Pediatric Allergy & Immunology Specialist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 164114 Pediatric Allergy & Immunology Specialist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 850140 Category: Faculty and Physicians 21633948 Responsibilities The Department of Pediatrics is seeking an outstanding individual for the Allergy and Immunology Division at the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center and Children’s Health Dallas. This position is focused upon expansion of clinical programs related to pediatric food allergy and general allergy. The applicant is expected to devote the majority of his/her time to patient care at the Fairview and Plano campuses. She/he may also participate in education of residents and fellows and advocacy efforts. Applicants must be eligible for medical licensure in the state of Texas and be board eligible or certified in Allergy and Immunology. Potential candidates should apply online at https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ and upload a curriculum vitae and a letter of interest. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression,