    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/21129086/molecular-physiologist-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Molecular Physiologist",
      "description": "Molecular Physiologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Molecular Physiologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 154914 Molecular Physiologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 784956 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 21129086 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Touchstone Diabetes Center, is seeking an Assistant Professor on the Tenure-Accruing Track. The position requires an M.D./Ph.D. or Ph.D. in basic science and 2-5 years postdoctoral research experience in an endocrinology related field. We are looking for a candidate specializing in metabolic disease with an in-depth insight into its impact on obesity and diabetes. As part of this specialty occupation, the individual will be responsible for conducting experiments with complex whole body physiology experiments. The expectation of this work will provide results that will significantly advance the understanding of the physiological responses to lipid and glucose metabolism as well as hormones, inflammation, and cancer. Additional duties will include the teaching and training of graduate students, house staff and fellows. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment... The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Touchstone Diabetes Center, is seeking an Assistant Professor on the Tenure-Accruing Track. The position requires an M.D./Ph.D. or Ph.D. in basic science and 2-5 years postdoctoral research experience in an endocrinology related field. We are looking for a candidate specializing in metabolic disease with an in-depth insight into its impact on obesity and diabetes. As part of this specialty occupation, the individual will be responsible for conducting experiments with complex whole body physiology experiments. The expectation of this work will provide results that will significantly advance the understanding of the physiological responses to lipid and glucose metabolism as well as hormones, inflammation, and cancer. Additional duties will include the teaching and training of graduate students, house staff and fellows. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishment and experience. Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a fu