      "title": "Molecular Physiologist",
      "description": "Molecular Physiologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Molecular Physiologist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 154913 Molecular Physiologist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 784955 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 21059709 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Touchstone Diabetes Center, is seeking an Assistant Professor with Tenure-Accruing Track. The position requires an M.D./Ph.D. or Ph.D. in basic science and 2-5 years postdoctoral research experience in an endocrinology related field. We are looking for a candidate specializing in adipose tissue biology and metabolic disease with an in-depth insight into its impact on in vitro models of human adipocyte subtypes. The individual will be responsible for conducting experiments taking advantage of an expanded adipose atlas to include additional depots and states. The expectation of this work will provide results that will significantly advance the understanding of the physiological responses to changes in cellular composition during weight gain and loss, in both mice and humans. We expect the candidate to be proficient in bioinformatics. Additional duties will include the teaching and training of graduate... The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Internal Medicine, Touchstone Diabetes Center, is seeking an Assistant Professor with Tenure-Accruing Track. The position requires an M.D./Ph.D. or Ph.D. in basic science and 2-5 years postdoctoral research experience in an endocrinology related field. We are looking for a candidate specializing in adipose tissue biology and metabolic disease with an in-depth insight into its impact on in vitro models of human adipocyte subtypes. The individual will be responsible for conducting experiments taking advantage of an expanded adipose atlas to include additional depots and states. The expectation of this work will provide results that will significantly advance the understanding of the physiological responses to changes in cellular composition during weight gain and loss, in both mice and humans. We expect the candidate to be proficient in bioinformatics. Additional duties will include the teaching and training of graduate students, house staff and fellows. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. Appointment rank will be comm