      "title": "Pediatric Pulmonology Physician",
      "description": "Pediatric Pulmonology Physician job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonology Physician job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 154654 Pediatric Pulmonology Physician Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 733408 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 21029207 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Pediatrics, is seeking outstanding individuals to join the Division of Pediatric Pulmonology and Sleep Medicine at UT Southwestern and Children’s Health Dallas. Eligible applicants will join the growing Pediatric Pulmonology and Sleep Medicine Division, which typically covers two hospital or consult services. Faculty members also work in outpatient Pulmonary clinics at Children’s Health. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Consultations that arise from the Pediatric Intensive Care Unit, Pediatric Cardiac Intensive Care Unit, tertiary level NICU, and general and subspecialty are