    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/22650969/assistant-professor-non-tenure-track-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Non-Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Non-Tenure Track) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Assistant Professor (Non-Tenure Track) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Open Menu Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 728894 Assistant Professor (Non-Tenure Track) Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 728894 Category: Faculty and Physicians 22650969 Responsibilities UT Southwestern Medical Center, Department of Urology, is seeking a full-time researcher in adult/pediatric urology. Qualified candidates will have appropriate education and training (Ph.D and/or M.D.) in relevant biological and engineering disciplines. The applicant must have an interest in teaching residents, fellows, and medical students in a university setting and will be expected to work closely with the newly created Bladder Center with a select focus on immunology. Competitive salary and benefits will be commensurate with qualifications. For consideration, please forward a cover letter and curriculum vitae to: Claus G. Roehrborn, M.D. Professor and Chair, Department of Urology UT Southwestern Medical Center 5323 Harry Hines Blvd. Dallas, TX 75390-9110 Phone: 214-648-2941 Fax: 214-648-4789 claus.roehrborn@utsouthwestern.edu Consideration may be given to applicants seeking less than a full-time schedule. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources/ This position is security-sensitive and subject to T