    "https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/job/22650884/medical-physicist-dallas-tx/": {
      "title": "Medical Physicist",
      "description": "Medical Physicist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Medical Physicist job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Locations Life in Dallas Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 625327 Medical Physicist Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 625327 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 30+ Days Ago 22650884 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The Department of Radiation Oncology at UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a Medical Physicist to fill an academic faculty position within the Division of Medical Physics and Engineering. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience.  Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree in Medical Physics or a related field and postdoctoral training and a minimum of 5 years working experience in the field of medical physics.  Candidate must be ABR certified. Excellent track record of research and successful funding history in the field of medical physics is required. Expertise in either small animal imaging and irradiation research or artificial intelligence is highly desired. The ideal candidate should have strong technical and communication skills along with commitment to technical and translational research. The individual sought will participate in the teaching of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows and residents. Personal attributes such as... The Department of Radiation Oncology at UT Southwestern Medical Center is seeking a Medical Physicist to fill an academic faculty position within the Division of Medical Physics and Engineering. Appointment rank will be commensurate with academic accomplishments and experience.  Applicants must have a Ph.D. degree in Medical Physics or a related field and postdoctoral training and a minimum of 5 years working experience in the field of medical physics.  Candidate must be ABR certified. Excellent track record of research and successful funding history in the field of medical physics is required. Expertise in either small animal imaging and irradiation research or artificial intelligence is highly desired. The ideal candidate should have strong technical and communication skills along with commitment to technical and translational research. The individual sought will participate in the teaching of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows and residents. Personal attributes such as motivation, initiative, problem-solving, and teamwork are highly desired for this position. The medical physicist is expected to participate in and provide needed clinical support to the research activities in the Department. Research projects in the Division of Medical Physics and Engineering, funded by various federal and state agencies including eleven active NIH R01 grants, range from small-animal irradiation, PET instrumentation, medical imaging, image-guided therapy, heavy ion therapy, and automatic treatment planning to artificial intelligence. An example research effort in our division is the MAIA Lab ( www.utsouthwestern.edu/labs/maia ). This position is security-sensitive and subject to Texas Education Code 51.215, which authorizes UT Southwestern to obtain criminal history record information. To learn more about the benefits UT Southwestern offers, visit https://www.utsouthwestern.edu/employees/hr-resources UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community. As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. Read less Read more Benefits Benefits UT Southwestern is proud to offer a competitive and comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees. Our benefits are designed to support your overall wellbeing, and include: PPO medical plan, available day one at no cost for full-time employee-only coverage 100% coverage for preventive healthcare – no copay Paid Time Off, available day one Retirement Programs through the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) Paid Parental Leave Benefit Wellness programs Tuition Reimbursement Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Qualified Employer Learn more about these and other UTSW employee benefits! Working at UTSW Bring Your “A” Game. Why are top candidates in so many professional fields – including customer service, finance, and human resources, to name a few – choosing UT Southwestern Medical Center as a career home? Simple. They know that they will work among a team of people who bring their best every day to support a health organization that’s breaking new ground in dozens of ways. That’s what we can offer you. It takes a lot to keep UT Southwestern at the forefront, where world-class patient care, acclaimed medical education, and innovative research breakthroughs are common occurrences. When you join us, those are the challenges you’ll share. Our organization has taken on serious commitments and responsibilities within a rapidly evolving health care system. Change is a constant, so our work supporting this complex matrix of business and systems needs must rise to the highest level of professionalism, collaboration, and innovation. That’s true for every role across the Medical Center and represents why this can be the most challenging work of your career. Share Share on Facebook (Opens in a new window) Share on Twitter (Opens in a new window) Share on Linkedin (Opens in a new window) Share by Mail Search Results Current Employees (Opens in a new window) Let’s Get Started Thank you for filling out the form. First Name * Last Name * Email * City City entered successfuly State State entered successfuly Country Country entered successfuly Area of Interest Area of Interest entered successfuly Administrative/Clerical Advanced Practice Provider Allied Health Campus Services Clinical Faculty and Physicians Finance Hospital Based Nurses Housekeeping Information Technology Insurance/Billing Nurse Educators Nursing Nutrition Professional & Executive Research & Laboratory Skilled Trade/Facilities Mgmt. Yes, I agree to the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy * No, I do not wish to be contacted with marketing and job alerts from UT Southwestern Medical Center. Remember Me Continue to Apply © 2026 Symphony Talent Terms of Use | Privacy Join Talent Community (Opens in a new window) Similar Opportunities Pediatric Endocrinology Physician Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Pediatric Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine Physician Scientist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Instructor - Neurology Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Leukemia Specialist Faculty and Physicians Dallas, TX Employee Testimonials Vanessa Pantoja Vanessa Pantoja GME Program Coordinator Dallas is the perfect size city for me. There are always amazing things to do in Dallas, from visiting the arts district, to museums, concerts, sporting events, and the state fair. Brenda Edwards. B