      "description": "OB/Gyn Gynecology Physician (Clements University Hospital) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX OB/Gyn Gynecology Physician (Clements University Hospital) job at UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, TX Skip to main content Sitemap Hide Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Life in Dallas Locations Frisco Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants Open Menu Why Work Here Military & Veterans Culture & Values Life in Dallas Locations Frisco Texas Behavioral Health Center Departments Advanced Practice Providers Adult Pediatrics Allied Health Faculty Imaging Services Information Technology Nursing Pharmacy Professional Services Research Postdoctoral Training Program Residencies & Fellowships Benefits Job Search Join Talent Community Log In Talent Community Sign In Current Employees Previous Applicants 196295 OB/Gyn Gynecology Physician (Clements University Hospital) Location: Dallas , TX Location Type: Job Number: 984203 Category: Faculty and Physicians Posted 2 Days Ago 24058930 Responsibilities Benefits Working at UTSW Responsibilities The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, Texas, seeks to fill a faculty position in the Division of Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery and Gynecology (MIGS). The successful candidate will have a passion for teaching and providing evidence-based clinical care.  Principal clinical assignment will be to provide clinical coverage and obstetrics and gynecological services at the UT Southwestern William P. Clements Jr. University Hospital and university-based ambulatory clinic sites, as well as teaching and mentoring to our students, residents and fellows. Qualification: Candidates must have an M.D. degree; completed an accredited residency in Obstetrics and Gynecology; and have attained or be eligible for Texas medical licensure and certification by the American Board of Obstetrics & Gynecology. Application Instructions: Interested candidates should apply online at https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ (Job# 984203)... The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, Texas, seeks to fill a faculty position in the Division of Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery and Gynecology (MIGS). The successful candidate will have a passion for teaching and providing evidence-based clinical care.  Principal clinical assignment will be to provide clinical coverage and obstetrics and gynecological services at the UT Southwestern William P. Clements Jr. University Hospital and university-based ambulatory clinic sites, as well as teaching and mentoring to our students, residents and fellows. Qualification: Candidates must have an M.D. degree; completed an accredited residency in Obstetrics and Gynecology; and have attained or be eligible for Texas medical licensure and certification by the American Board of Obstetrics & Gynecology. Application Instructions: Interested candidates should apply online at https://jobs.utsouthwestern.edu/ (Job# 984203) and upload a curriculum vitae, letter of interest and contact information for three references. UT Southwestern Medical Center is committed to an educational and working environment that provides equal opportunity to all members of the University community.  As an equal opportunity employer, UT Southwestern prohibits unlawful discrimination, including discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, or veteran status. This position is securit